.TH "SCCFM-CLI INVENTORY DEVICES ASA SHUN REMOVE" "1" "2026-08-19" "0.39.1" "sccfm-cli inventory devices asa shun remove Manual"
.SH NAME
sccfm-cli\-inventory\-devices\-asa\-shun\-remove \- Remove one or more shun entries from ASA...
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sccfm-cli inventory devices asa shun remove
[OPTIONS]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Remove one or more shun entries from ASA devices. Repeat --source-ip to remove multiple IPs in a single transaction.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-n,\fP \-\-device\-name TEXT
Device name to search for (supports wildcards like 'branch-*').
.TP
\fB\-q,\fP \-\-query TEXT
Filter devices by a Lucene query.
.TP
\fB\-l,\fP \-\-limit INTEGER RANGE
Maximum records to return  [default: 50; 1<=x<=200]
.TP
\fB\-o,\fP \-\-offset INTEGER RANGE
Pagination offset  [default: 0; x>=0]
.TP
\fB\-u,\fP \-\-device\-uids TEXT
List of device UIDs to remove the shun from.
.TP
\fB\-\-source\-ip\fP TEXT
Source IP to remove from the shun list. Repeat to remove multiple IPs in one transaction.  [required]
.TP
\fB\-\-check\fP
Run a preflight check without performing the operation.
.TP
\fB\-\-wait\fP / \-\-no\-wait
Wait for the transaction to finish before returning.  [default: no-wait]
.TP
\fB\-\-format\fP [table|json]
Output format  [default: table]
.TP
\fB\-\-config\-path\fP PATH
Path to the configuration file (defaults to ~/.sccfm-cli/config.json).
